WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.401 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Congratulations.
You have written,

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:02.235 line:92%
you star in a Christmas film

00:00:02.235 --> 00:00:04.738 align:start size:94% position:6%
You are in one of the most
beloved Christmas films

00:00:04.738 --> 00:00:06.339 line:92%
of all time, "Love Actually.

00:00:06.339 --> 00:00:07.841 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, yes.
-Yeah.

00:00:07.841 --> 00:00:08.708 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:08.708 --> 00:00:09.743 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You're adding --
-I had forgotten.

00:00:09.743 --> 00:00:12.245 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You're adding to the canon,
which is very nice.

00:00:12.245 --> 00:00:14.514 line:92%
You must like a Christmas film

00:00:14.514 --> 00:00:15.915 line:92%
-Yeah, I like some of them

00:00:15.915 --> 00:00:17.250 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. That's true.
-I like some of them.

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:18.752 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's some real duds
out there.

00:00:18.752 --> 00:00:23.089
-Yeah. Yeah, though, it's no
common to get a really good one.

00:00:23.089 --> 00:00:24.691 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I did feel
we needed a new one.

00:00:24.691 --> 00:00:27.727 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You did -- Okay,
so this was out of necessity

00:00:27.727 --> 00:00:28.561 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:28.561 --> 00:00:31.965 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think necessity
is putting it too strongly

00:00:31.965 --> 00:00:32.399 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:00:32.399 --> 00:00:34.167 size:75% position:38%
-Although I did need
to earn some money.

00:00:34.167 --> 00:00:36.069 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right, right.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:36.069 --> 00:00:38.538 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that is what Christmas
is all about.

00:00:38.538 --> 00:00:41.041 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-Is all about, people.

00:00:41.041 --> 00:00:42.575 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Let's not forget.

00:00:42.575 --> 00:00:43.309 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:43.309 --> 00:00:46.079 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I don't want skip over
a very interesting detail.

00:00:46.079 --> 00:00:47.614 align:start size:94% position:6%
You wrote this film
with your husband.

00:00:47.614 --> 00:00:48.882 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I did.
-And you've never written

00:00:48.882 --> 00:00:50.350 align:start size:94% position:6%
a film together before.
-No.

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:52.285 size:75% position:38%
-That must have been
a lovely experience.

00:00:52.285 --> 00:00:54.054 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was, and it was
accidental, as well,

00:00:54.054 --> 00:00:56.856 align:start size:94% position:6%
because -- because
this wonderful producer

00:00:56.856 --> 00:01:00.260 align:start size:94% position:6%
David Livingston said, "Do you
feel like writing a movie

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:03.596 align:start size:94% position:6%
based on George Michael's
Wham! song, 'Last Christmas'?"

00:01:03.596 --> 00:01:05.398 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I said, "Not really."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:05.398 --> 00:01:09.536
Because I'm not -- It's no
my favorite Christmas song

00:01:09.536 --> 00:01:10.103 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:01:10.103 --> 00:01:11.538 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And, um,
it was a long time ago.

00:01:11.538 --> 00:01:13.273 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I listened to it,
and I thought,

00:01:13.273 --> 00:01:14.574 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Last Christmas,
you gave me your heart.

00:01:14.574 --> 00:01:16.576 align:start size:94% position:6%
Then the very next day,
you gave it away.

00:01:16.576 --> 00:01:18.478 align:start size:94% position:6%
And this year --"
What can I do that?

00:01:18.478 --> 00:01:19.779 line:92%
I can't think of a story.

00:01:19.779 --> 00:01:21.081 size:81% position:41% line:92%
So, I told my old man.

00:01:21.081 --> 00:01:23.850 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we were on a walk
in the hills in Scotland.

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:24.517 size:88% position:44% line:92%
And we thought, I wonder

00:01:24.517 --> 00:01:27.287 align:start size:94% position:6%
if there's something else
we could do with it.

00:01:27.287 --> 00:01:30.156 align:start size:94% position:6%
Could we come at it
at a different angle?

00:01:30.156 --> 00:01:34.928 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, we started
dreaming up this idea.

00:01:34.928 --> 00:01:35.862 size:88% position:44% line:92%
You start with the idea,

00:01:35.862 --> 00:01:37.831 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is like
a little piece of grit.

00:01:37.831 --> 00:01:38.932 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And then you have to

00:01:38.932 --> 00:01:41.434 align:start size:94% position:6%
kind of pearlize the grit
over many years

00:01:41.434 --> 00:01:44.471 size:81% position:41%
with draft after draft
after draft, you know?

00:01:44.471 --> 00:01:47.140 align:start size:94% position:6%
But the idea was good,
and it lasted.

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:50.944 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I met George Michael
about it

00:01:50.944 --> 00:01:52.979 line:92%
two years before he died.

00:01:52.979 --> 00:01:55.248 size:81% position:41% line:92%
And what a lovely guy.

00:01:55.248 --> 00:01:57.217 line:92%
-Yeah. And I will say, I -

00:01:57.217 --> 00:01:59.352 align:start size:94% position:6%
Which is a thing
that I always regret,

00:01:59.352 --> 00:02:01.287 align:start size:94% position:6%
I almost feel as though
I appreciated

00:02:01.287 --> 00:02:03.723 align:start size:94% position:6%
exactly how lovely he was
after he passed away.

00:02:03.723 --> 00:02:05.592 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I totally agree.
-You sort of hear the tributes

00:02:05.592 --> 00:02:08.194 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you realize,
"Oh. I sort of saw you

00:02:08.194 --> 00:02:11.030 align:start size:94% position:6%
through the prism
of your pop culture persona.

00:02:11.030 --> 00:02:12.132 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-"And you were so much more --

00:02:12.132 --> 00:02:14.134 align:start size:94% position:6%
There was so much more depth
to you than that."

00:02:14.134 --> 00:02:15.502 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, he was
an extraordinary man.

00:02:15.502 --> 00:02:17.604 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, really on the search
all his life

00:02:17.604 --> 00:02:19.506 align:start size:94% position:6%
for a kind of authentic
way of being.

00:02:19.506 --> 00:02:22.408
'Cause he hadn't come out
for a long, long time,

00:02:22.408 --> 00:02:23.676 line:92%
and that was really hard.

00:02:23.676 --> 00:02:28.414
And his move from that
kind of Wham! music to --

00:02:28.414 --> 00:02:31.551
Like, "Listen Without Prejudice"
is one of the greatest album

00:02:31.551 --> 00:02:32.952 size:78% position:39% line:92%
of all time, I think.

00:02:32.952 --> 00:02:34.821 size:84% position:42% line:92%
And I didn't realize --

00:02:34.821 --> 00:02:35.522 size:78% position:39% line:92%
It was really spooky.

00:02:35.522 --> 00:02:39.926 align:start size:94% position:6%
I had no idea how pertinen
his lyrics, his poetry,

00:02:39.926 --> 00:02:43.930 align:start size:94% position:6%
and his music were to the movi
and the story in the movie

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:47.967 size:84% position:42%
until -- It was like
that late, late arrival

00:02:47.967 --> 00:02:49.102 size:88% position:44% line:92%
like you just described.

00:02:49.102 --> 00:02:49.802 line:92%
I just went, "Oh, my God.

00:02:49.802 --> 00:02:53.039 align:start size:94% position:6%
This guy's really deep
and profound

00:02:53.039 --> 00:02:56.676 align:start size:94% position:6%
and had very, very
great things to say

00:02:56.676 --> 00:02:57.477 line:92%
about what it is to be human

00:02:57.477 --> 00:02:59.979 align:start size:94% position:6%
and how difficult it is
and how complicated it is.

00:02:59.979 --> 00:03:03.249
-When you get a message like
that from the work you're --

00:03:03.249 --> 00:03:05.318 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, this is not
an adaptation of a song,

00:03:05.318 --> 00:03:07.387
but the song is the inspiration,
somebody else's work.

00:03:07.387 --> 00:03:09.589 align:start size:94% position:6%
When you get that from them,
are you so excited?

00:03:09.589 --> 00:03:10.590 align:start size:94% position:6%
'Cause you're, like,
"Oh, my God.

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:11.991 size:81% position:41%
They had given me more
than I even thought"?

00:03:11.991 --> 00:03:15.228
Or do you have fear of, like
"Oh, I better not blow this,

00:03:15.228 --> 00:03:18.665
'cause now this is more than
I thought it was going to be"?

00:03:18.665 --> 00:03:21.601 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It happened over
such a long period of time

00:03:21.601 --> 00:03:23.369 align:start size:94% position:6%
-How many years was it?
-Eight.

00:03:23.369 --> 00:03:24.871 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Eight years?
-Yeah.

00:03:24.871 --> 00:03:25.638 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Wow.
-Yeah.

00:03:25.638 --> 00:03:28.474 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That you guys --
your marriage survived

00:03:28.474 --> 00:03:32.078
working on an eight-year project
of any kind.

00:03:32.078 --> 00:03:34.581 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. Absolutely.
It's extraordinary, isn't it

00:03:34.581 --> 00:03:35.748 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's the real
Christmas miracle.

00:03:35.748 --> 00:03:37.884 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, I mean, any long-term
relationship, yeah.

00:03:37.884 --> 00:03:40.486 align:start size:94% position:6%
You just go,
"How is it possible?"

00:03:40.486 --> 00:03:43.323 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's basically impossible,
actually.

00:03:43.323 --> 00:03:45.758 align:start size:94% position:6%
So you just go --
Every moment that it lasts

00:03:45.758 --> 00:03:48.394 align:start size:94% position:6%
you go, "Well,
this is kind of impossible

00:03:48.394 --> 00:03:51.698 line:92%
But it still seems to be here.

00:03:51.698 --> 00:03:53.299 size:75% position:38% line:92%
Wow, how fantastic."

00:03:53.299 --> 00:03:55.401 align:start size:94% position:6%
And just keep
your fingers crossed.

00:03:55.401 --> 00:03:56.135 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-When did you shoot it?

00:03:56.135 --> 00:03:58.304 size:84% position:42%
Because there's so much
Christmas decorations

00:03:58.304 --> 00:04:00.073 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the film.
Was it past Christmas?

00:04:00.073 --> 00:04:03.276
Was it before? In real life,
when you were shooting it.

00:04:03.276 --> 00:04:04.544 line:92%
-Well, the fortunate thing was

00:04:04.544 --> 00:04:08.081 align:start size:94% position:6%
that we were shooting in Londo
at night, before Christmas

00:04:08.081 --> 00:04:10.450 align:start size:94% position:6%
three weeks before Christmas
Great. All great.

00:04:10.450 --> 00:04:12.585 align:start size:94% position:6%
Everyone -- Okay.
We started at 2:00 A.M.,

00:04:12.585 --> 00:04:14.654 align:start size:94% position:6%
so, in Covent Garden,
and it was magical, magical.

00:04:14.654 --> 00:04:18.024
And everyone's, "Oh, guys, it'
Christmas. It's so gorgeous.

00:04:18.024 --> 00:04:19.759 line:92%
And then we had Christmas,

00:04:19.759 --> 00:04:21.361 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we were thinking,
"This is great.

00:04:21.361 --> 00:04:23.329 align:start size:94% position:6%
We get two weeks off
for Christmas,"

00:04:23.329 --> 00:04:23.997 size:81% position:41% line:92%
forgetting, of course,

00:04:23.997 --> 00:04:27.634 align:start size:94% position:6%
that Christmas is so
unbelievably exhausting.

00:04:27.634 --> 00:04:29.135 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.
-So, everyone came back

00:04:29.135 --> 00:04:30.203 line:92%
afterwards -- "Oh, I'm so tired.

00:04:30.203 --> 00:04:32.071 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was a really [bleep]
Christmas.

00:04:32.071 --> 00:04:33.006 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I had a row with --

00:04:33.006 --> 00:04:35.141 align:start size:94% position:6%
Long-term relationships
are impossible."

00:04:35.141 --> 00:04:35.875 size:84% position:42% line:92%
Blah, blah, blah, blah.

00:04:35.875 --> 00:04:38.911 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then we had to carry o
doing Christmas.

00:04:38.911 --> 00:04:40.413 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Until February!

00:04:40.413 --> 00:04:41.614 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Ugh!
[ Laughter ]

00:04:41.614 --> 00:04:43.383 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, that is
just a nightmare.

00:04:43.383 --> 00:04:45.918
-A nightmare.
-You were that terrible neighbor

00:04:45.918 --> 00:04:47.987 align:start size:94% position:6%
that doesn't take
their decorations down.

00:04:47.987 --> 00:04:49.355 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Ugh!
[ Laughter ]

00:04:49.355 --> 00:04:51.958 align:start size:94% position:6%
-In England, do --
Because we go from Halloween

00:04:51.958 --> 00:04:54.994
and then we have a little bi
of a break with Thanksgiving

00:04:54.994 --> 00:04:56.195 size:75% position:38% line:92%
that you don't have.

00:04:56.195 --> 00:04:58.097 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is it just pretty much
straight Christmas

00:04:58.097 --> 00:04:59.866 line:92%
from Halloween on over there

00:04:59.866 --> 00:05:00.667 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-From about July.

00:05:00.667 --> 00:05:02.702 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, from July.
-Yeah, about then.

00:05:02.702 --> 00:05:04.837 line:92%
-You're a Christmassy culture?

00:05:04.837 --> 00:05:05.571 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Terrible.
-Yeah.

00:05:05.571 --> 00:05:08.374 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, it's not -- I mean,
culture's just the wrong word.

00:05:08.374 --> 00:05:10.243 align:start size:94% position:6%
When they start
selling Christmas,

00:05:10.243 --> 00:05:13.179 align:start size:94% position:6%
they start selling it fast
and very early.

00:05:13.179 --> 00:05:15.682 size:88% position:44%
-They come right at you.
-Yeah, and I'm, like --

00:05:15.682 --> 00:05:16.783 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
With our family,

00:05:16.783 --> 00:05:19.952 align:start size:94% position:6%
I like Christmas,
because I had a nice childhood

00:05:19.952 --> 00:05:20.386 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Uh-huh.

00:05:20.386 --> 00:05:23.823
-So, I start sticking cloves
into fruit around November

00:05:23.823 --> 00:05:27.093
And my husband, who did no
have a very nice childhood

00:05:27.093 --> 00:05:30.963
really wants to be placed
into some medically induced coma

00:05:30.963 --> 00:05:34.100 align:start size:94% position:6%
around December 15th
to January 1st.

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:35.835 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, just, like,
put on a drip or something

00:05:35.835 --> 00:05:37.870 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, talking of
long-term relationships,

00:05:37.870 --> 00:05:39.405 size:75% position:38% line:92%
it's taken 25 years.

00:05:39.405 --> 00:05:41.674 size:81% position:41%
You know how you get
a hedgehog to come in?

00:05:41.674 --> 00:05:43.976
just open the back door
and leave a saucer of milk there

00:05:43.976 --> 00:05:46.479
and hope that it finds --
-I'm going to pretend I do

00:05:46.479 --> 00:05:48.414 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:48.414 --> 00:05:50.650 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's a small mammal.
-Okay, yeah.

00:05:50.650 --> 00:05:51.851 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We don't have any left,
of course,

00:05:51.851 --> 00:05:53.686 align:start size:94% position:6%
because of climate change,
and Brexit, as well.

00:05:53.686 --> 00:05:57.123
They all packed their little -
their little mammals rucksacks

00:05:57.123 --> 00:05:59.125 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, oh, really?
-And -- Yeah, they just left

00:05:59.125 --> 00:06:01.194 align:start size:94% position:6%
They said, "We don't
need to be here anymore."

00:06:01.194 --> 00:06:02.028 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-They were pro-stay.

00:06:02.028 --> 00:06:03.963 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. "There won't be
any spare food.

00:06:03.963 --> 00:06:05.698 align:start size:94% position:6%
And people will start
eating us again."

00:06:05.698 --> 00:06:07.734
-It's interesting, 'cause
I was in Italy this summer

00:06:07.734 --> 00:06:09.569 size:88% position:44%
and there were so many
more hedgehogs than I --

00:06:09.569 --> 00:06:11.204 size:75% position:38%
-Yeah, just -- Yeah.
-They've emigrated.

00:06:11.204 --> 00:06:13.439 align:start size:94% position:6%
-With their little packs.
-And they had British accents.

00:06:13.439 --> 00:06:15.041 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They're gone, yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:15.041 --> 00:06:17.443 line:92%
Their little hedgehog passports.

00:06:17.443 --> 00:06:18.211 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Squeaking ]

00:06:18.211 --> 00:06:21.147
-Which is hard for -- I feel bad
for the immigration people

00:06:21.147 --> 00:06:23.850 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause to me,
all hedgehogs look alike.

00:06:23.850 --> 00:06:25.418 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:06:25.418 --> 00:06:27.987 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And their passports
are so tiny.

00:06:27.987 --> 00:06:30.423 align:start size:94% position:6%
You have to have
those tiny stamps.

00:06:30.423 --> 00:06:31.591 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:31.591 --> 00:06:32.792 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Squeaking ]

00:06:32.792 --> 00:06:34.193 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
"There you go.

00:06:34.193 --> 00:06:36.796 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Bye. Enjoy France."

00:06:36.796 --> 00:06:38.164 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know what?
I'm going to end it here,

00:06:38.164 --> 00:06:40.066 align:start size:94% position:6%
only 'cause I never want peopl
to find out

00:06:40.066 --> 00:06:42.702 align:start size:94% position:6%
what your hedgehog analogy
was going to be.

00:06:42.702 --> 00:06:45.138 align:start size:94% position:6%
I want them always to be like,
they got so sidetracked

00:06:45.138 --> 00:06:46.572 align:start size:94% position:6%
that we never knew
why Emma was saying,

00:06:46.572 --> 00:06:49.342 align:start size:94% position:6%
"You know how you lure in
hedgehogs with water?

00:06:49.342 --> 00:06:52.512 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you've got your mallet
Anyway --"

00:06:52.512 --> 00:06:53.446 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:06:53.446 --> 00:06:55.648 line:92%
That's Emma Thompson, everybody.

